    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Vilazodone = ⍉a first-line agent per Canadian guidelines ← lack of head-to-head or relapse data and need to titrate and take w food."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "1"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -12,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 2,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "b.",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "tabPt": 12
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "italic"
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Auvelity "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "(US) contains bupropion and dextromethorphan.  Dextromethorphan = an NMDA (N-methyl-D-aspartate) receptor antagonist, but its mech in depression = unclear."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "32"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "  Bupropion boosts dextromethorphan levels via CYP2D6 inhibition."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "32"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "  There = ⍉proof that dextromethorphan alone = effective for depression.  There = ⍉proof that "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "italic"
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Auvelity "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "= better than standard-dose bupropion (ex, bupropion 150 mg twice or 300 mg QD).  "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "italic"
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Auvelity "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "use w other dextromethorphan-containing prod (ex, cough or cold medicine) could cause neuropsych SE (ex, psychosis, stupor, seizures)."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "32"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "  Serotonin syndrome could result from extra dextromethorphan use, or "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "italic"
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Auvelity "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "use w serotonergic drugs (ex, linezolid, serotonergic antidepressants)."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "32,33"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -12,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 2,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "c.",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "tabPt": 12
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 10.6
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "Wholesale Acquisition Cost (WAC).  Med pricing by Elsevier, accessed January 2024."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -12,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 2,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "d.",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 12
        }
       }
      ],
      "tabPt": 12
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Limited available evidence suggests that abruptly switching (ie, direct switch) from one "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "short-acting "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "SSRI or SNRI to another SSRI or SNRI = generally well-tolerated."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "3,7,10"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Transient serotonergic side effects (ex, anxiety) may occur early in the switch, but this = ⍉USU a safety issue, and a direct switch = USU better tolerated than a washout if the first agent = short-acting.  "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "TAPERING/CROSS-TAPERING "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(ie, gradually increasing the new agent [often starting w a lower dose than usual] while decreasing the first agent):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "22"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Tapering may be more appropriate in some cases ← two concerns when switching:  Sx recurr and discontinuation syndromes."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "12,30"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Discontinuation syndromes are of most concern when switching from a serotonergic agent to a nonserotonergic agent, particularly when switching "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "from venlafaxine "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "or "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "paroxetine"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "2,7"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Consider tapering any antidepressant taken for more than one wk."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "27"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Fluoxetine and bupropion may ⍉need tapering."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "6,26,27"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  For others, consider tapering over several wks unless there = a clin reason ⍉ to."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "30"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Monitor pt and adjust switching strategy (ex, speed of taper) based on Sx of w.draw, side effects, or return of depressive Sx."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "2,10"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Consider increasing the dose of the serotonergic agent if w.draw Sx emerge (ex, “GI flu”-like Sx, paresthesias, irritability, insomnia, dizziness, vivid dreams)."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "10"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Individual Sx could also be treated (ex, meclizine for dizziness)."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       },
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 12
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "27"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  A resource for switching = "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "size",
        "attrs": {
         "pt": 12
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "https://switchrx.com/antidepressants.php/switch"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -12,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 2,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "e.",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 12
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Gepirone ["
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "italic"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Exxua"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", US] = a selective serotonin 5HT1A-r agonist."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "44"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  It has ⍉been shown to be more effective than other antidepressants, and = more expensive than generic first-line agents.  Long-term data = limited.  Common SE incl dizziness, nausea, and HA."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "44"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " It requires baseline and periodic electrocardiographic monitoring ← risk of QT prolongation, and has sig interactions w CYP3A4 inhibitors."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "44"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "  Additionally, dose adjustments are required for older adults and for pts w kidney or liver impairment."
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "vertAlign",
        "attrs": {
         "value": "sup"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "44"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
